{title: Another Advocate}
{subtitle: John 14:16–18; 14:26–27; Acts 2:1–4}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 98}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm7] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
On [Bb]the night before he suffered, in [F/A]an upper room [Gm7]they sat
With [Bb]the bread upon the table [F/A]and their hearts were full of [Gm7]fear
He said, [Bb]I am going to the Father, [F/A]but you will not be [Gm7]alone
And [Eb]he spoke a word of promise [F]for the days when he'd be [Bb]gone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will ask the [Eb]Father, and he will give you an[Bb]other Ad[F]vocate
To be with you for[Eb]ever
The Spirit of [Bb][F]truth
I will not [Eb]leave you as or[F]phans; I am coming to [Eb]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When the [Bb]day of Pentecost had come, they [F/A]were all together in one [Gm7]place
Suddenly a sound came from heaven like a [Eb]rushing, violent wind
[F]Tongues as of fire appeared to [Gm7]them
They [Eb]were all filled [F]with the Holy Spir[Bb]it
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will ask the [Eb]Father, and he will give you an[Bb]other Ad[F]vocate
To be with you for[Eb]ever
The Spirit of [Bb][F]truth
I will not [Eb]leave you as or[F]phans; I am coming to [Bb]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
But the Ad[Eb]vocate, the Ho[F]ly Spirit
[Gm7]Whom the Father [Bb]will send in my [Eb]name
Will teach you [F]all things
And remind [Gm7]you of everything [Bb]I have said to [Eb]you
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]I will not [Eb]leave you as or[F]phans
I am coming to [Eb]you
{end_of_verse}
